    assignment in a service.d override does NOT clear the inherited
    Conflicts=getty@tty1.service from phosh.service's own unit file, even
    after `systemctl daemon-reload` - `systemctl show phosh.service -p
    Conflicts` kept showing getty@tty1.service, and manually starting
    getty@tty1.service actually stopped phosh.service, proving the
    conflict was still enforced. The real fix now lives in the phosh
    package itself (r7 fork, +r7phosh1: Conflicts=getty@tty1.service
    removed at the source), where it's confirmed to work.

